Paradox Faction Codex

Faction Lore
The Paradox Faction exists in the spaces between truth and falsehood, reality and illusion. They are masters of contradiction, wielding the power of the Knot of Eternity to bend causality itself. Their warriors do not simply fight—they rewrite the very nature of battle, making lies into truth and truth into weapons. Born from the spiraling world of Yith, where time coils upon itself, they understand that reality is merely a suggestion to be edited at will. Their technology defies logic, their tactics confound reason, and their very presence on the battlefield makes certainty impossible. They fight not to destroy their enemies, but to prove that victory was always inevitable—even when it wasn't.

Faction Warcry
Temporal Paradox: Once per game, at the start of any phase, you can declare this ability. Choose one friendly unit that was destroyed this turn. That unit is immediately restored to the battlefield at half strength (rounded down), placed anywhere more than 6 cm from enemy units. This unit gains the Never Was rule until the end of the turn (cannot be targeted by enemy abilities or attacks, but also cannot affect the game in any way).

Faction Abilities
Reality Glitch (1 CP): Use at the start of any phase. Choose one friendly unit. Until the end of the phase, that unit counts as being in two places at once—it can act from both its current position and any point within 12 cm of its current location.
Causal Loop (2 CP): Use during your opponent's turn. Choose one enemy unit that just made an attack. That attack never happened—reverse all effects and return the game state to before the attack was declared.
False Truth (1 CP): Use when an enemy unit declares a charge against one of your units. That unit is actually charging a different friendly unit of your choice within 18 cm instead.
Temporal Echo (3 CP): Use during your turn. Choose one friendly unit. It can act twice this turn, but the second action must be exactly identical to the first.
Paradox Field (2 CP): Use at the start of any phase. Choose one terrain feature or objective marker. It doesn't exist this turn, but will return at the end of the turn.

Faction Blessings
You can choose two of these blessings to give to any units in your army. Remember, a single unit can only receive one blessing.
Blessing of Uncertainty: When this unit is attacked, roll a D6. On a 5+, the attack was aimed at a different unit (opponent's choice) within 6 cm instead.
Blessing of Contradiction: This unit can move through solid terrain and other units as if they don't exist, but must end its move in a legal position.
Blessing of the Impossible: Once per turn, this unit can re-roll any single dice roll (including opponent's rolls that target this unit).
Blessing of Retroactive Victory: If this unit is destroyed, roll a D6. On a 6, it was never destroyed and remains at 1 wound.
Blessing of the Maybe: This unit's weapons have a 6+ chance to ignore armor saves entirely, regardless of AP value.

Keywords
Caster: A unit with this keyword can attempt to manifest psychic powers during the Psychic Phase.
Psychic Power: A special ability that requires a Caster to use. It must be manifested by rolling psychic dice to meet or exceed its casting value.
Torrent: A weapon with this keyword automatically hits its target.
Assault: A weapon with this keyword can be fired even if the unit advanced this turn.
Heavy: A weapon with this keyword can be fired once per turn. If the unit remains stationary, it gains +1 BS and WS this turn.
Melee: A weapon used in close combat.
Core: A basic unit type that forms the backbone of your army.
Character: A unique, named unit, often with special abilities.
Warlord: The designated leader of your army.
Paradox: The faction keyword for all units in this codex.
Mirage: When this unit is targeted, roll a D6. On a 4+, the attack targets a different unit within 6 cm instead.
Temporal: This unit can act in previous phases—declare actions during deployment that take effect later.
[CONFUSION]: Enemy units within 6 cm of this unit subtract 1 from hit rolls.
[MISDIRECTION]: When this unit is attacked, the attacker must roll a D6. On a 4+, they attack themselves instead.
Deep Strike: Able to access the reserves.
Fly: Can move over terrain and other models.

